# Hospital Prescription
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Hospital — one drug prescribed as part of a Medical Record
# Case 20 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: hospital-medical-record.menata
#
# Split out from hospital-medical-record.menata (corrected 2026-07-11): originally an
# inline `Table of (...)` field. Already fully expressible as an ordinary Object
# References pattern (001-object.md §Relationships) — "a Medical Record has many
# Prescriptions" is implied by "each Prescription references one Medical Record," no
# separate grammar needed. Clinical decision support (drug interaction checks, dosage
# limits) stays out of scope here, same boundary the parent file draws.

Prescription

Fields

- Medical Record : Medical Record
- Drug Name : Text
- Dosage : Text
- Frequency : Text
- Duration : Duration

Constraints

- Drug Name is required.
- Dosage is required.

Permissions

Clinician

- Create
- View

Views

- Prescription List : List
- Prescription Detail : Detail
